    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d563">

                <pb facs="0482" n="366" xml:id="pg366"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 838.516/14.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">New York</hi></placeName>, [<date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content-and-sibling-dates"
                            calendar="gregorian" notAfter="1914-12-10T23:59:59-05:00"
                            notBefore="1914-12-09T00:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >undated</hi></date><hi rendition="#italic">; received December 10,
                            1914.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Referring to our letter of December 8 and telegram to Haiti bank attached to said
                    letter, please substitute for said telegram the following: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>From total gold you hold, retain four hundred thousand dollars there.
                            Have balance packed for shipment uninsured to Hallgarten by United
                            States warship. You will be advised later name ship and date sailing.
                            Cable immediately amount you will ship. Send by first mail all
                            statements condition bank, also statements customs receipts since June
                            30.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wehrhane</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
